there's no doubt that avengers end game  was one of the most successful superhero  films of all time wrapping up so many  different character arcs that spread  over a decade of movies  there's one scene near the end of the  film though that's led fans to develop a  crazy theory that captain america steve  rogers is actually mr rogers welcome  back everyone to stream in the galaxy my  name is rocket riley and today we're  going to be talking about the fan theory  that the mcu's captain america is mr  rogers but before we get started if  you're new to the channel please hit the  subscribe button and click the bell icon  to be notified when we upload a new  video now avengers endgame saw the final  chapter of several different marvel  characters stories including iron man  black widow and captain america the mcu  saga started with tony stark a  self-centered billionaire who grew into  a father willing to sacrifice everything  for the greater good as iron man  black widow or natasha romanov also  sacrificed herself to help get the soul  stone and to defeat thanos  one of the craziest changes though  happened in some of the final scenes of  the movie steve rogers was tasked with  returning the infinity stones to their  own timelines in order to prevent a  complete collapse in the multiverse and  strands of time held in place by the tva  and the sorcerer supreme doctor strange  some of what steve did when he went back  in time could be seen as a contributing  factor to the cataclysmic events that'll  be shown in spider-man no way home and  doctor strange and the multiverse of  madness  fans have even come up with a movie idea  for marvel studios titled captain  america the last mission where he has to  overcome obstacles to return the  infinity stones before settling down  with peggy carter this film could also  give some more clarity into how steve  could actually become fred rogers  when steve went back in time using the  pym particles we assumed that he placed  the infinity stones back in their  respective timelines before traveling to  the 1940s to live with his one true love  peggy  we even see a scene at the end of  avengers end game of steve dancing  slowly with peggy finally settling down  after years of war and fighting other  people's battles this fan theory  suggests that due to his natural desire  to do good and his near perfect moral  compass steve wasn't able to just stay  at home raising his family i don't see  him being able to go to work in a 9-5  normal job after saving the world  countless times and facing the threats  he's had to throughout his career  instead he had to go out and do  something meaningful with his life  spreading positivity in the world  changing his first name to fred but  keeping his surname rogers in the scene  where steve gives the iconic shield and  mantle of the captain america name to  sam wilson he doesn't tell sam about his  life he just says  this is beautiful  this certainly leaves his life from the  1940s to the present day up to  interpretation  it seems as if he's almost purposely not  telling sam about his past in order to  cover up his true identity steve wanted  to share his wisdom and ideals with the  rest of the world so he became the  unforgettable mr rogers hosting the  educational children's television show  mr rogers neighborhood which ran from  1968 to 2001.  steve now named fred decided to live the  life that was taken away from him when  he sacrificed it all in the first  captain america film  not only is this something steve has  wanted his whole life it's something he  deserves after all he's given to the  world and the best part is he's not done  giving to the world he continues to  share kindness and wholesome messages to  children around the world all while  fulfilling his dream of being with peggy  once again  this theory is pretty believable because  we know how good-natured steve rogers is  and we know how willing he is to help  people in need steve held grief  counseling sessions following the snap  and avengers end game using his years of  wisdom to help give people clarity and  closure in their lives this just shows  how steve wanted to help spread  positivity and to change people's lives  for the better just as mr rogers did  with his television show  the two also look quite similar with  almost identical hairstyles and skin  tones the resemblance is pretty uncanny  between the two of them the only issue  in the theory is that steve was born in  1918 and fred was born in 1928. one  could probably say that cap seemed to  age more slowly because of the super  soldier serum so he looked like he might  have been born in 1928 and so he just  fudged some medical records when he  changed his name  it's hard to think of any other flaws in  this theory that can't be fixed with  just a bit of extra storytelling  if steve did actually become fred rogers  when he stayed back in the 40s he only  did so because he believed he could make  a greater impact on people by doing so  rather than by fighting wars although  captain america did have a knack for  beating all odds and winning against  powerful global threats his superhuman  capabilities have always come second to  the reason he was actually chosen for  the super soldier program in the first  place  get away  get back  [Music]  is this a test  both captain america and mr rogers hold  a special place in many people's hearts  and the thought of them being the same  person in an alternate reality gives a  certain level of closure to the  character of steve rogers that we didn't  really get an avengers end game plus  it's fun to think of kind mr rogers  having superhuman strength and access to  thor's hammer mjolnir just thinking of  the two individuals being the same  person brings a smile to my face and i  hope to see more wholesome theories like  this in the future  well that's gonna be everything from us  today on the captain america mr rogers  theory if you enjoyed the video please  hit the like button and don't forget to  subscribe for more great content what  are your thoughts about this theory are  there any other details which further  prove its truth drop your thoughts in  the comment section below  from everyone here at stream of the  galaxy we hope you have a great day and  thanks for watching
 

